# Build context excludes for packages/server/Dockerfile.
#
# BuildKit reads `<dockerfile>.dockerignore` in preference to the root
# .dockerignore, so this file governs `docker build -f packages/server/Dockerfile .`
# It lives beside the Dockerfile on purpose: sync-oss.sh mirrors packages/ to the
# public repo but does not sync root-level files, so a root .dockerignore would
# silently rot out of the OSS mirror.
#
# The Dockerfile also copies by explicit path rather than `COPY . .`, so these
# entries are a second line of defence — and what keeps a local build from
# shipping a 1.1 GB context.

**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.turbo
**/.vitepress/cache
**/.vitepress/dist

# Never let a developer's local secrets reach the build context: cli.ts runs
# `import 'dotenv/config'` from the working directory.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

.git
.github
run_logs
**/*.log
